<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Brenmil half year share dips on maize price.</title>
<headline>Brenmil half year share dips on maize price.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     6.2	   vs 11.3</p>
<p>    Operating profit	1.73	  vs 4.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.24	  vs 4.11</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.78	  vs 1.47</p>
<p>    Interest		  0.51 gain   vs 0.27 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  66.46	 vs 63.48</p>
<p>Full name: Brenner Mills Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African maize miller Brenmil said that a rise in the price of maize due to a crop shortage had pressurised its margins. Lost production and sales due to industrial action also hit profit.</p>
<p>The group said the current maize crop had been satisfactory and prices had come down. This would see earnings improve in the second half, but the full year figures are not expected to equal those of last year, the firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
